==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_OperationsRespectPermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OperationsRespectPermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the model invent a Customer-role caller invoking GetAudit, which is denied by the permission matrix and forbidden to customers in FR-002/FR-021. The injection forces exactly that operation to exist.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_002_CustomerPermissions, FR_021_OfficerIdentityHidden
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_CustomerPermissions: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_021_OfficerIdentityHidden: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoDuplicateAuditEntries  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_NoDuplicateAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing the no-duplicate-events fact lets the model construct two distinct ApplicationEvent atoms recording the same applied transition on the same application. The injection forces this duplication so the AppendOnly invariant has something to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AppendOnlyAudit
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_018_AppendOnlyAudit: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Removing the partial-unique-index fact lets a single customer hold two simultaneous in-flight applications. The injection forces two distinct Submitted applications owned by the same customer, which the FR-008 assertion is designed to reject.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecidedByEqualsAssignedOfficer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecidedByEqualsAssignedOfficer.als
    rationale: Removing the decided-by-equals-assigned fact lets a Decision atom record a deciding officer different from the application's assigned officer. The injection forces an Approved application whose decision.decidedBy is not the assignedOfficer, violating FR-013.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides
      - FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEntryExistsForEveryTransition  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditEntryExistsForEveryTransition.als
    rationale: Removing the audit-existence fact lets an Approved application exist without any newStatus=Approved event recording the decision transition. The injection forces exactly this missing-entry instance, which AuditCompleteness must catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_019_ExactlyOneEntryPerAppliedTransition
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_ExactlyOneEntryPerAppliedTransition: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppCustomerIsCustomerRole  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AppCustomerIsCustomerRole.als
    rationale: Removing the customer-role-of-customer fact lets a LoanApplication be owned by a User whose role is LoanOfficer or ComplianceReviewer, breaking the ownership-role pairing that FR-005 and OwnershipExclusivity rely on.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_005_CustomerIdentityFromAuth
      - OwnershipExclusivity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_CustomerIdentityFromAuth: FAIL (expected)

